# Copy to .production.vars (untracked: `cf/**/.production.vars*` is git-ignored) and fill in the PUBLIC values of the
# PRODUCTION API and admin Worker `sakem-admin` (cutover Phase A, docs/cloudflare/cutover-runbook.md section 14).
# `pnpm deploy:prod:command` reads it and PRINTS the deploy command with every value passed as --var; it does not deploy.
# Copied as it is, this file is refused: the placeholder must be replaced.
#
# Public values only. Secrets (BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY) are never written here: they go in
# with `pnpm exec wrangler secret put <NAME> --env=""`, typed at its prompt. Nothing here may look like staging: no
# workers.dev, no r2.dev, no resend.dev sender, no Turnstile TEST key (1x00...).

# The PUBLIC site key of the REAL Turnstile widget (the same one the public site uses: its hostname list includes
# sakolakembara.org, which covers admin.sakolakembara.org). The matching secret key is a secret of this Worker.
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=<site key of the production widget>

# The public origin of the files bucket (a custom domain on the PUBLIC bucket, never r2.dev), no trailing slash.
UPLOADS_BASE_URL=https://files.sakolakembara.org

# The origin of the public site, for the "Lihat di publik" link of a published article.
SITE_URL=https://sakolakembara.org

# Only if a Resend key is set (invitation, verification and reset mails): the From, on the domain verified in Resend.
# Without a Resend key leave it out: those mails fail closed (503).
# EMAIL_FROM=Sakola Kembara <no-reply@sakolakembara.org>
